## Step 2: Identify Non-Dominated (Pareto-Front) Candidates

For two objectives (maximize Modulus, maximize Pore Fraction), a point is non-dominated if no other point is ≥ on both objectives and strictly better on at least one.

Sorting by Pore Fraction descending to find the Pareto front:

- PF=0.43: 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2 run1 → Modulus=350.75 (single specimen, unreliable)
- PF=0.39: 18-15deg-600s-NoN2 run1 → Modulus=476.82 (top gap defect, but measured)
- PF=0.37: 19-10deg-240s-NoN2 run2 → Modulus=308.88 (single specimen)
- PF=0.36: 17-10deg-60s-N2 → Modulus=381.81; 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1 → 519.51; 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run4 → 501.80
- PF=0.35: 17p5-5deg-550s-N2 run2 → 342.50 (high CV); 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run5 → 529.63
- PF=0.34: 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run5 → 529.63
- PF=0.33: multiple ~400-570 range
- PF=0.32: multiple ~400-600 range
- PF=0.31: 547.22, etc.
- PF=0.30: 596.31, 675.14
- PF=0.29: 640.23
- PF=0.28: 596.34, 708.94 (run1 single), 777.89 (top gap)
- PF=0.27: 591.97, 640.23 (run2)

**Constructing the Pareto front** (keeping only non-dominated points with reliable measurements):

Starting from highest PF:
- (476.82, 0.39) — 18-15deg-600s-NoN2 run1: dominated by anything with Modulus≥476.82 AND PF≥0.39? No such point exists → **Pareto front**
- (519.51, 0.36) — 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1: not dominated by (476.82, 0.39) since 519.51>476.82 → **Pareto front**
- (529.63, 0.34) — 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run5: 529.63>519.51 → **Pareto front**
- (596.31, 0.30) — 18-5deg-180s-N2: 596.31>529.63 → **Pareto front** (single specimen though)
- (675.14, 0.30) — 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 run2: 675.14>596.31, same PF → **Pareto front**
- (640.23, 0.29) — 17-15deg-90s-N2 run2: dominated by (675.14, 0.30) since 675.14>640.23 AND 0.30>0.29 → **dominated**
- (591.97, 0.27) — 17-15deg-90s-N2 run1: dominated by (675.14, 0.30) → **dominated**

So the reliable Pareto front candidates are:
1. **(476.82, 0.39)** — 18-15deg-600s-NoN2 (run1 only, top gap defect)
2. **(519.51, 0.36)** — 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1 (one of three runs)
3. **(529.63, 0.34)** — 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run5 (one of five runs)
4. **(675.14, 0.30)** — 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 run2 (two runs with very different values: 936.62 vs 675.14 vs 601.17)

