## Step 4: Strategy Assessment

The current Pareto front (reliable, multi-specimen):
- **(529.63, 0.34)** from 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 runs 4&5 — reasonably confirmed
- **(675.14, 0.30)** from 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 run2 — only one good-quality run

The key question: **Can we find a point with Modulus >529 AND PF >0.34?** That would be a true Pareto improvement.

**Observations about the landscape:**
- Higher bath temperature (15-20°C) tends to give higher PF (0.32-0.36)
- Lower bath temperature (5-10°C) with polymer_wt=17-17.5 gives higher modulus but lower PF
- The 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 condition sits between these: bath_temp=18 gives moderate PF but high modulus in run2
- The 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 condition (bath_temp=20) gives PF~0.34-0.35 with Modulus~500-530

**Gap in the space**: Between bath_temp=18 (PF~0.27-0.30, Modulus~600-675) and bath_temp=20 (PF~0.34-0.35, Modulus~500-530), there may be a sweet spot around bath_temp=19 that could yield both higher modulus AND higher pore fraction than either confirmed point.

Also worth noting: **17p5-18deg-75s-N2 run2** at (675.14, 0.30) is only one good-quality run. Run3 gave (601.17, 0.20) — very different PF. This needs validation before treating as confirmed Pareto front.

**Decision**: The 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 condition has high uncertainty (run2 PF=0.30 vs run3 PF=0.20, both single specimens). Before exploring new territory, I should consider whether to:
1. Validate 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 (uncertain Pareto candidate)
2. Explore bath_temp=19 as a potential Pareto improvement

Given that runs 4&5 of 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 are reasonably consistent (PF=0.34-0.35, Modulus=500-530), and 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 run2 shows (675, 0.30) but run3 shows (601, 0.20), the 18deg condition is **not confirmed**. A third run at 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 would help, but run3 already exists (though single specimen with PF=0.20).

Actually, looking more carefully: runs 2 and 3 of 17p5-18deg-75s-N2 both have measurements but give very different PF (0.30 vs 0.20). This is high variability and the condition is not confirmed as a reliable Pareto point.

**Best action**: Explore bath_temp=19°C with polymer_wt=17.5, which sits between the confirmed (529, 0.34) at bath_temp=20 and the uncertain (675, 0.30) at bath_temp=18. This could potentially yield a Pareto improvement (higher modulus than 529 with PF>0.34, or higher PF than 0.34 with modulus>529). The wait time of 75s (used at bath_temp=18) vs 90s (used at bath_temp=20) — I'll use 75-90s range. Other parameters: mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=10, N2=True, nips_bath_wait_time=1800.

This is a new, unexplored condition that could yield a Pareto improvement in the gap between two known Pareto-front regions.

